# Who reviews what.
#
# Ownership is path-scoped rather than repository-scoped, which is the point of keeping metadata and
# source-hosted packages in one repository: a package's maintainer reviews their own directory
# without gaining rights over the registry's machinery.

# The registry's own machinery: schemas, CI, and the rules everything else is validated against.
/schemas/           @Descolada
/.github/           @Descolada
/README.md          @Descolada
/CONTRIBUTING.md    @Descolada
/CODEOWNERS         @Descolada

# Packages maintained by the project itself, including ports of scripts with no upstream repository.
/packages/keysharp/ @Descolada

# Per-owner lines go below, added when an author claims their imported packages. Until then the
# organisation holds them: everything under packages/ falls back to this.
/packages/          @Descolada
